I have now read all 7 TypeScript source files, plus `package.json` and `tsconfig.json`. Here is the complete performance analysis.

---

## Performance Issues Report: `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server`

---

### ISSUE 1 [CRITICAL -- Memory Leak]: Unbounded cache growth with no size limit or periodic cleanup

**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/utils/CacheManager.ts`, lines 3-81

The `CacheManager` class uses a `Map` with no maximum capacity. New entries are added on every fresh GitHub file fetch or component lookup, and they are never evicted except when accessed after expiry (lazy cleanup at `get()` lines 19-21 and `has()` lines 53-56). The `cleanup()` method (lines 62-69) exists but is **never called** automatically -- it is only invoked inside `getStats()` (line 74). A long-running MCP server that serves many distinct component queries will accumulate every distinct file in memory indefinitely.

**Fix:** (1) Enforce a max size (e.g., `maxSize: 500`) with LRU or least-recently-used eviction on `set()`. (2) Call `cleanup()` on a timer in the constructor and clear the timer in a `destroy()` method:

```typescript
constructor() {
  this.cache = new Map();
  this._cleanupTimer = setInterval(() => this.cleanup(), 300000); // every 5 min
}
destroy() { clearInterval(this._cleanupTimer); }
```

(3) Also call `this.cleanup()` periodically from `set()` when size exceeds some threshold.

---

### ISSUE 2 [HIGH -- Redundant Nested Computation]: `getComponentDependencies()` does O(N*M*K) work, called once per component on every listing

**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/ReactBitsService.ts`, lines 157-170

```typescript
private getComponentDependencies(slug: string): string[] {
  const deps: string[] = [];
  for (const [dep, categories] of Object.entries(componentHealth.dependencies)) {
    if ((categories as string[]).some((cat: string) => {
      const categoryData = (componentHealth.componentHealth as any)[cat];
      return categoryData?.components && slug in categoryData.components;
    })) {
      deps.push(dep);
    }
  }
  return deps;
}
```

This method is called on **every component** during `listComponents()` (line 190). Inside it:
- It iterates all dependency entries (6 entries)
- For each, `.some()` iterates the dependency's category list (up to 3 categories)
- For each category, it does a property lookup in the nested `componentHealth` object

This is called for 135+ components, and the data (`componentHealth`) is completely static. The result is always the same for a given slug.

**Fix:** Pre-build a reverse lookup `Map<string, string[]>` in the constructor:

```typescript
private depsBySlug: Map<string, string[]>;

constructor() {
  this.depsBySlug = new Map();
  for (const [dep, categories] of Object.entries(componentHealth.dependencies)) {
    for (const cat of categories as string[]) {
      const catData = (componentHealth.componentHealth as any)[cat];
      if (catData?.components) {
        for (const slug of Object.keys(catData.components)) {
          if (!this.depsBySlug.has(slug)) this.depsBySlug.set(slug, []);
          this.depsBySlug.get(slug)!.push(dep);
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Then replace the method body with: `return this.depsBySlug.get(slug) ?? [];`

