### ISSUE 3 [HIGH -- Sequential HTTP Requests on Failure]: Alternative path fallback is serial instead of parallel

**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/ReactBitsScraper.ts`, lines 18-41

When the primary URL returns a 404, the scraper tries 7 alternative paths **one at a time** using `for...of` with `await`:

```typescript
const altPaths = [
  `/text-animations/${componentSlug}`,
  `/animations/${componentSlug}`,
  // ... 5 more
];
for (const path of altPaths) {
  try {
    const response = await axios.get(`${this.baseUrl}${path}`);
    return response.data;
  } catch (e) {
    // Continue trying other paths
  }
}
```

Each request must wait for the previous one to complete or fail. In the worst case this is 8 sequential HTTP round-trips before the component is reported as not found. Each request bound to the default axios timeout (which is unset -- see Issue 4) could take 30+ seconds.

**Fix:** Fire all alternative paths in parallel and take the first success:

```typescript
const promises = altPaths.map(path =>
  axios.get(`${this.baseUrl}${path}`).then(r => r.data)
);
return await Promise.any(promises);
```

(Note: `Promise.any` is ES2021+, which is covered by the project's `target: "ES2022"`.)

---

### ISSUE 4 [HIGH -- No HTTP Timeout]: Axios requests have no timeout set

**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/GitHubService.ts`, line 32
**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/ReactBitsScraper.ts`, lines 11, 32

The `GitHubService` creates an axios instance without a `timeout`:

```typescript
this.api = axios.create({
  baseURL: 'https://api.github.com',
  headers: { ... }
  // timeout is missing
});
```

The `ReactBitsScraper` uses bare `axios.get()` calls with no timeout either. If GitHub or reactbits.dev hangs, the request blocks the MCP tool call indefinitely. There is no abort signal passed from the MCP layer either.

**Fix:** Add a timeout to both:

```typescript
this.api = axios.create({
  baseURL: 'https://api.github.com',
  timeout: 15000,  // 15 seconds
  headers: { ... }
});
```

And in the scraper:

```typescript
const response = await axios.get(url, {
  timeout: 15000,
  headers: { 'User-Agent': '...' }
});
```

