### ISSUE 6 [MEDIUM -- Duplicate Cache Instances]: Two separate `CacheManager` instances with no shared eviction

**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/ReactBitsService.ts`, line 148
**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/GitHubService.ts`, line 29

Both `ReactBitsService` and `GitHubService` create their own separate `new CacheManager()` instances. This means two completely independent in-memory caches with separate size limits and TTLs. Memory pressure in one cache has no effect on the other. A single LRU-aware cache shared between both would yield better overall memory efficiency.

**Fix:** Create the `CacheManager` at the `ReactBitsService` level and pass it to `GitHubService` and `ReactBitsScraper` via constructor injection:

```typescript
constructor() {
  this.cache = new CacheManager();
  this.scraper = new ReactBitsScraper(this.cache);
  this.github = new GitHubService(githubToken, this.cache);
}
```

