### ISSUE 11 [LOW -- No AbortSignal Propagation]: Long-running HTTP requests have no cancellation path from MCP tool layer

**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/index.ts`, lines 121-229
**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/GitHubService.ts`, lines 47-79
**File:** `/home/arrafi/reactbits-mcp-server/src/services/ReactBitsScraper.ts`, lines 8-41

The MCP SDK does not pass cancellation signals to tool handlers, but if the client disconnects or times out, there is no mechanism to abort in-flight HTTP requests. The axios calls will continue executing until they resolve or hit their own timeout. Combined with the missing timeout in Issue 4, this means a disconnected client cannot stop wasted HTTP requests.

**Fix:** When/if the MCP SDK adds `AbortSignal` to `CallToolRequest`, thread the signal through to axios via `{ signal }`. For now, at minimum add timeouts (see Issue 4).

